# device_info_descriptor_argbuf_off: Config fields that reach the device info: argument buffers (key 33 bit 0x20, key 42) need isolation and are on unless the config disables them, so disabling them turns them off under isolation and enabling them changes nothing without it; a memory map sets key 33's large-task bits, which the blocks setup lacks. "protected" is the default config: it once set Apple's enableProtectedContent, which was never read and which the C API does not have.
